61	122	\N	2024-12-23 12:45:44.72	58.50	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/2\\\\147\\\\SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "24-02-2025 10:30:07", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>How much time do we spend using smartphones each day without noticing their impact on our lives ?</p>\n<p>The growing reliance on smartphones has sparked debates about their benefits and drawbacks.</p>\n<p>This essay will focus on the key benefits smartphones provide and their downsides.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Smartphones have revolutionized the communication by making it instant, easy, quickly and accessible, allow people to stay connected no matter where there are. For exemple, smartphones enable families separated by great distances to maintain a close relationships.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>While smartphones offer undeniable advantages, they also come with significant downsides that cannot be ignored. For instance, excessive use lead to addiction, social isolation and reduced productivity etc ...</p>\n<p>Although smartphones have downsides, their positive potential cannot be overlooked and overall benefits far outweigh the negatives. For instance, smartphones give access to online education, helping people to learn and grow.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>In the end, it is not the technologies but how we use them that defines their impact on our lives, if we use them wisely, they can improve our live, if not, they may harm us.</p>\n<p>So, let us strive to use smartphones responsibly, maximazing their benefis while minimazing their drawbacks.</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
