82	122	\N	2024-12-23 12:46:48.65	73.00	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/2\\\\131\\\\SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "24-02-2025 11:26:23", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sustainable developpement has long been a subject of debate, reflecting its focus on economic growth, environmental protection and social equity. This essay will explore that climate change is a shared responsabilities in the world between developed and poorer nations to address various challenges related to these areas for both current and future generations.</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Firstly, all countries will shift to renewable energy in order to redude reliance on fossil fuels and stimulate job creation, while eco-friendly infrastruture attracts investments and ensures long-term stability. This action promotes economic growth by fostering innovation and creating green jobs. &nbsp;For instance, Germeny's investments have created over 300,000 jobs and reduce greenhouse gas emmissions, highlight the significant economic potentiel for sustainable practices.</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;In addition, climate change is a shared responsability between all countries in the world, applying sustainable developpement preserves ecosystems and biodiversity by managing resouces responsibly. Using renewable energy reduces carbon emmissions and combats climate change. Moreover, Sustainable agriculture protects natural habits and minimizing deforestation, while waste reduction and recycling help prevent pollution and conserve ressources.</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Furthermore, these responsabilities ensures that all individuals have fair access to resources, opportunities and rights, regardless their background. It seeks to reduce disparities in race, gender and incoming promoting inclusivity and justice. This can be achieved through policies that focus on education, healthcare, employment and legal equal protection addressing inequalities and enabling succes of all.</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;However, critics argue that solve the problem of climate change is related to United States and some nations in the developping world.&nbsp; The strict environmental regulations may slow economic growth, increase costs, limit job creations and reduce productivity&nbsp; in poor countries especially&nbsp;in industries like manufactering and fossil fuels.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;While these concerns are valid, the resolution of climate change offers long-term benefits and stability. For instance, countries uses renewable energy reduces reliance on fossil fuels and creates green jobs in order to protect the environment&nbsp; and the society.</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; In conclusion, by sharing responsabilities on climate change and investing on renewable energy, sustainability can protect environmental for both current and future generations.</p>\n<p style="padding-left: 40px;">&nbsp;</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	1
