13	1	2	en	1	<span style=&apos;font-size: 15px&apos;>For some, the key to resilience is physical activity, for others it is mental activity, or emotional activity, or social activity.</span><br/><span style='color:#a6a6a6; font-style: italic'>Note: In this case we are speaking about psychological resilience defined by the ability of an individual to psychologically support the trials of life.</span>	Enseignant de langue, communication et citoyenneté
13	1	2	en	2	<span style=&apos;font-size: 15px&apos;>Europeans are so accustomed to posing as champions of democracy and considering Human Rights as their main, if not their only, distinctive and common credo that they unconsciously consider the words Europe and democracy to be synonymous.</span><br/><span style='color:#a6a6a6; font-style: italic'>Alain Lancelot June 2002.</span><br/><br/><span style=&apos;font-size: 14px&apos;>What do you think about this now in 2024?.</span>	Enseignant de langue, communication et citoyenneté
